 "posture": "Friday's session was a broad AI-capex shakeout, not a narrow one: the S&P 500 fell 1.8% below its 100-day average and the Nasdaq 2.9% to a three-month low, while VIX jumped 12.9% to 19.42 — still inside the normal 16–20 band. Breadth scores 44.6/100 (Neutral), with the 8-day breadth MA at 0.605 in a 200-day downtrend and a muted bearish signal active; the model's equity-exposure band is 60–75%. Inside the collector's 75-stock universe only 35 names sit above their 50-day average and 44 above their 200-day — selective, deteriorating, not broken. Crypto reads 63.2/100 Neutral (5 of 6 components): BTC is a bull pullback between its 50- and 200-day averages but 30% below its 1-year high, funding is near baseline, and only 10% of the top-20 are positive over 30 days. With the 10-year at 4.93% and December hike odds near 72–75%, rate-sensitive assets stay under pressure.",
 "sentiment": "Risk-off, concentrated where capital intensity is highest: the market is repricing AI spend against cash flow (Alphabet's worst day since IPO, Intel's worst since 1974) even as energy and parts of the broad tape held up. The week ahead adds midterms and payrolls, so expect headline-driven volatility to stay elevated.",
